{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition","id":1563206,"title":"First time ST, best starting hangouts for my Coterie? (first/second edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-17T18:38:05-07:00","id":1563206,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> First time ST, best starting hangouts for my Coterie? (first/second edition)","content":"Hey all,<br /> <br /> First time Storyteller here. Gonna be starting my chronicle this weekend and I needed some help. My players have been vampires for a little while, just under a full year or so. I can easily finagle a reason theyd all work together (venture, tremere, nosforatu), but where would they hang out exactly?<br /> <br /> Are Elysium's always in effect as hang out spots? Are there vampire run clubs or secret places mostly vamps frequent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","user":"Internetflexing","date":". 08-18-2026, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-17T21:57:30-07:00","id":1563208,"title":"","content":"Usually pcs belong to the same coterie. A coterie is the equivalent of a dnd party. A small group of vampires who work together.<br /> A coterie can be formed for many reasons. Security, some mutual work that needs to be done, pooling of skills and assets.<br /> <br /> A coterie does not have to be created by its members, younger vampires may find themselves in a coterie decided for them by their sires or by older vampires they are beholden to.<br /> <br /> Coteries are expected to hang together. Move across town in a group or at least two by two.<br /> <br /> Elysium or a favored hunting ground (the Rack) are common places vampires can meet each other but it can get cumbersome in play to always go to a place with other npcs to talk about stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","user":"Tjalei","date":". 08-19-2026, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T02:24:58-07:00","id":1563216,"title":"","content":"Maybe a place similar to the Succubus Club.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T06:42:58-07:00","id":1563221,"title":"","content":"That's mostly a thing for the players to decide.<br /> <br /> Vampires usually take care of their own business, they keep in contact but &quot;hanging out&quot; among themselves isn't a regular widespread activity. It happens, but more as a case by case thing.<br /> <br /> Elysium is a common partial exception, but it is more a &quot;neutral ground&quot; than necessarily a hangout. What makes Elysia is the Keeper being able and wiling to both keep it open for all vampires but rigid on enforcing rules. From this most Elysia have at least a few social events a month as a means to spread news and most days someone will be there for part of the night, but commonalities end here.<br /> <br /> Overall that's a thing for you to decide about your setting, your city. Are there popular hangouts for vampires? Some cities have, others don't. Some have many. In some your political allegiances say a lot of where you're likely to be, in others each clan has its own living space, for others spaces where factions meet each other to argue are the point. You do you here.<br /> <br /> Just remember that unless a more powerful vampire is ordering them around, characters can have very personal tastes and takes on all this. Assuming everyone frequents a given space because that's normal is a very good way to piss off some player. Either force things in game through a bossy older vampire or let them figure out what they want themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T04:17:57-07:00","id":1563246,"title":"","content":"Many of those questions sadly are best answered with: it depends. <br /> <br /> Elysium is a term for a neutral ground. But it can mean either a permanent fixture or just ad hoc decision. An art gallery where Toreador meet once a week can be Elysium as can be a conference hall that Prince hired for a weekend to host the meeting of all city vampires because of Sabbat infiltrator getting caught in his domain. <br /> <br /> At the end of the day the details are up to you to come up with. Is a local Brujah running an &quot;invite only&quot; bar/meeting place where all the local Kindred meet every night? Is a Toreador run opera hall frequented by Cainites who have a special entrance and a meeting room guarded by ghouls? There are multiple possibilities. <br /> <br /> As for why the coterie is working together it's the ages old question: why do PCs in RPG work together. And that is to you to come up with your players. Are they brought up by their patron/mawla? Are they part of some official group: Prince's strong arms, Justicar archons and so on? Or are they just brought together by events - they see something that they shouldn't have and now, in the crosshairs of dangerous enemy, they are banding together for safety in number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T11:29:26-07:00","id":1563254,"title":"","content":"I gotta ask for the setting for this one.<br /> <br /> Are you using a known city or an invented one? From there on I might give you a better insight.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T11:42:16-07:00","id":1563256,"title":"","content":"In the game I'm currently playing the ad-hoc meeting place is an arcade run by one of the PCs. Initially we were contacted by the local regents (the city is divided between two elders who are on good terms) and there would be no main meeting ground, but the Sheriff really liked the arcade and call us there regularly, so it kind of stuck.<br /> <br /> But it does help that out of 6 PCs, 4 are heavy on games: I'm a Tzimisce game developer, the place is from a Brujah nostalgic with arcades, we have a Lasombra videogame publisher and a Malkavian hacker Embraced as a child who's, well, a computer-using child, obviously she likes games.<br /> <br /> The Gangrel old lady is the only one who's not used to videogames and arcades, while the mortal cop is lazy enough in his work that he genuinely prefers to find excuses to hang with the undead in a vintage arcade.<br /> <br /> So, bottom line: the group will make the hangout, not the ST. If you want a reason for them to be in the same place at the same time, it's better to make a particular event for that than try to guess a common hangout.<br /> <br /> Ok. If in D&amp;D there's a classic air over the &quot;you met at a tavern&quot; starting point, I'd say the closer we get to it in Vampire is &quot;the Prince called for something&quot;. It may be a call for the PCs to give them work, but can also be a party where all in the Domain are expected to appear, or a public announcement, maybe the formal presentation where the Fledglings will be deemed Neonates. Bloodlines 1 had a good one with the execution of your sire as something almost every NPC in LA felt they should attend to.<br /> <br /> Whatever it is, the important part is putting the PCs in the same place to see the starting plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-21T20:03:06-07:00","id":1563326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition?p=1563254#post1563254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta ask for the setting for this one.<br /> <br /> Are you using a known city or an invented one? From there on I might give you a better insight.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Newark! This is set in the wake of the Camarilla driving out the heavy Sabbat Prescence and consolidating some power here. Current prince is a relatively young Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T12:49:55-07:00","id":1563347,"title":"","content":"Having a Giovanni prince can be a modern thing.<br /> This could drive the attention of Toreador and their antitribu when feeding in racks. Imagine the Prince inflicting pain while feeding, what does the victim feel when offered to him/her? What's the Toreador reaction towards it? Imagine the permissions requested to perform artistic representations of such act on both spheres of influence of the clan.<br /> <br /> Any Camarilla PC with a standing on its history might question the Promise of 1528. Why is there a Giovanni Prince and which Justicar/archon/Camarilla luminary permit it? Were the previous authority so incompetent? Here is another story seed towards the Camarilla structure. Perhaps the Ventrue PC's sire want to see his childe ruling (or himself/herself) after he/she do all the dirty work to pave the ground to it. Ventrue are all about lineage and prestige, having that in mind and that you are playing 1st/2nd ed, I have this idea. Remember Victoria Ash's original twist on her being a sort of medium (Giovanni Chronicles II)? Imagine your Ventrue PC being the one that actually motivated her to forget that nonsense and focus her on Camarilla status? Years later she is eligible for the princedom of NYC (which she eventually rejects; Clan Novel Saga) but having such a prestigious kindred on its pocket might bring here Succubus Club event to Newark, sponsored by the PCs.<br /> <br /> On' the Tremere PC angle there I suggest reading Clan Trilogy Tremere for story seeds (though I admit I never liked them), since it deals with the Tremere relation with the Baali. Aisling lost control of the chantry daemon and had visions of the &quot;children from the well&quot; (I interpret as the Baali organ pit of Ashur). Add Tzimisce under NYC an its probable intention to expand himself to Newark, since he already went ahead to Adirondack park (north) when Leopold fought the Gangrel and seriously crippled Xaviar (Clan Novel Gangrel) plus there are Anatole's scrawls in that cave. A boon might be called by Malkavian clanmates, or not since it destroyed those who read them to the Madame Guil (The Beast Within Revised novel). Lord Ephraim Wainwright (Nights of Prophecy, New York by Night) is an expert on music, therefore, communicating frequencies, any inquiries on the issue might be requested by him. If you want to include the VtM: Shadows of NY game story, you can add the Vritra factor on Lucien de Maupassant's death. Perhaps Aisling, the High Regent is still searching for the perpetrator (if any!). Her entry to NYC might clarify the mystery. On the Newark angle, is there a chantry there? Will the Tremere of NYC want to establish a chantry there? Perhaps the PC can be smart enough to open one there. There are two Tzimisce factors here, Lambach and Cysek (the latter one if you choose to include Gehenna book, which is not really good).<br /> <br /> Oh, on the Nosferatu PC. Augustyn, Calebros' sire, disappeared in search of the Inconnu. Perhaps the PCs is one of his contactts to evade attention and actually had the exclusive on his return with the answers. You PC now has the exclusive info that even Calebros don't know of yet. Also, here is another tie on the [Tzimisce] probably expansion westward.<br /> I'll explain the next thing from my head cannon POV. The Eldest rest under NYC, so, who brought him? My choice would be Ionache, childe of the Antediluvian and founder of the Voivode system, supposedly destroyed by the Arpad Ventrue during the formation of the Council of Ashes (Transylvania by Night, Players Guide to High Clans). It was here before the formation of New Amsterdam, therefore, someone brought the seed during or right after the colonization of America. Those known to travel before Columbus were Absimiliard, The Slumbering Giant, Tezcatlipoca, Xipe Totec, Menele and Shaitan. Imagine your Nosferatu PCs gaining exclusive info on this when the Nosferatu in general know nothing about? There's another story seed here, there were Nosferatu in America prior to its colonization (see Tlacique: Clanbook Followers of Set/Blood Sacrifice), what if they contact your PC on the info he/she is interested in? Will he share it with his clanmates?}<br /> <br /> I know all this is very canon story seeds and a lot reading might be required, but hope it helps.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T13:22:19-07:00","id":1563349,"title":"","content":"I particularly think offering too much canon is not good advice for an assumed first time ST with a homebrew city. It's throwing confusion on someone who's still grasping the basics.<br /> <br /> This is particularly problematic when you start already throwing high consistency expectation with things like the Promise and Justicar authorization. I don't know Internetflexing, but most first time STs I've seen and myself when I was one feel paralyzing fear with this kind of suggestion, because it sounds they're actually completely unprepared and doing it wrong and running them game requires tons of studying and mastery over and entire library of setting lore.<br /> <br /> Not want to be too harsh, but I've literally seen this kind of pressure, even just as suggestions, cripple chronicles and stop people from ever trying to ST. I'm meeting today a friend that has been trying to overcome one of those for the last 25 years. He's still preparing his game.<br /> <br /> A Giovanni as a Prince isn't anything to pay much heed. I don't see a Justicar wasting time with this if it isn't causing bigger problems, and if it is key it run in the chronicle. Any need for explanation may wait for later, maybe never happen. Kindred in the city may never know if is uncommon, or it may not be, since this is in 1st edition and most of this lore does not apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-22T18:12:15-07:00","id":1563353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition?p=1563347#post1563347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a Giovanni prince can be a modern thing.<br /> This could drive the attention of Toreador and their antitribu when feeding in racks. Imagine the Prince inflicting pain while feeding, what does the victim feel when offered to him/her? What's the Toreador reaction towards it? Imagine the permissions requested to perform artistic representations of such act on both spheres of influence of the clan.<br /> <br /> Any Camarilla PC with a standing on its history might question the Promise of 1528. Why is there a Giovanni Prince and which Justicar/archon/Camarilla luminary permit it? Were the previous authority so incompetent? Here is 