NYC want to establish a chantry there? Perhaps the PC can be smart enough to open one there. There are two Tzimisce factors here, Lambach and Cysek (the latter one if you choose to include Gehenna book, which is not really good).<br /> <br /> Oh, on the Nosferatu PC. Augustyn, Calebros' sire, disappeared in search of the Inconnu. Perhaps the PCs is one of his contactts to evade attention and actually had the exclusive on his return with the answers. You PC now has the exclusive info that even Calebros don't know of yet. Also, here is another tie on the [Tzimisce] probably expansion westward.<br /> I'll explain the next thing from my head cannon POV. The Eldest rest under NYC, so, who brought him? My choice would be Ionache, childe of the Antediluvian and founder of the Voivode system, supposedly destroyed by the Arpad Ventrue during the formation of the Council of Ashes (Transylvania by Night, Players Guide to High Clans). It was here before the formation of New Amsterdam, therefore, someone brought the seed during or right after the colonization of America. Those known to travel before Columbus were Absimiliard, The Slumbering Giant, Tezcatlipoca, Xipe Totec, Menele and Shaitan. Imagine your Nosferatu PCs gaining exclusive info on this when the Nosferatu in general know nothing about? There's another story seed here, there were Nosferatu in America prior to its colonization (see Tlacique: Clanbook Followers of Set/Blood Sacrifice), what if they contact your PC on the info he/she is interested in? Will he share it with his clanmates?}<br /> <br /> I know all this is very canon story seeds and a lot reading might be required, but hope it helps.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>bruh I had never heard of the promise that forbid the giovani from taking power in camarilla structures, im kinda screwed now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-23T02:47:03-07:00","id":1563361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Internetflexing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition?p=1563353#post1563353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> bruh I had never heard of the promise that forbid the giovani from taking power in camarilla structures, im kinda screwed now</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't take it too seriously. The details are quite hazy and on my a few novels and chronicles of partial canonicity put to much weight in it.<br /> <br /> There may exist a ton of possible reasons for a Giovanni to have managed this, and seriously most of the time a Prince isn't simply the one in the area strong enough to take power, and outsiders strong enough to do something about it have better things to do if it isn't causing trouble.<br /> <br /> You can learn more and come up with a reason for the exception later, and it will probably never be needed anyway, it'll just be a curiosity of your city.<br /> <br /> While technically the Promise was a biding oath taken centuries ago so the Camarilla would not interfere in Giovanni affairs at the time, the reality is that it's unknown if it has any serious intent. They didn't want to interfere with each other and the main goal of the pact was to have a justification if anyone else tried to complain, so it's perfectly possible that actual enforcement is nonexistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-01T18:55:10-07:00","id":1563778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Internetflexing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition#post1563206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can easily finagle a reason theyd all work together (venture, tremere, nosforatu), but where would they hang out exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many conceivable places where vampires would gather for all sorts of reasons.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the PC coterie itself, I suggest you ask them where they'd like to gather. That could be multiple locations depending on the reason. One might be a place that one or more of the PCs control where they could meet in private without any other people. Another could be a place open only to people who are a greater part of vampire society, and thus issues of the Masquerade aren't an issue. Maybe that location is a convenient spot where they could meet NPCs on a social basis, for discussing vampire politics, or to make deals. A third type of place might be a public or semi-public place where mortals ignorant of the Masquerade might also gather so it's important for the PCs to be careful what they say or do. However, such places could be useful in meeting their mortal Allies, Contacts, or people involved in their Influence.<br /> <br /> I call these kind of places &quot;sets&quot; like a theatre set. It's an established location where any PC can set a scene they want. Such places could be a fortified haven known to the other PCs; a place of business where a PC runs his empire; a private social club that is member's only; an expensive, elite restaurant that has special VIP rooms in back for the vampires; a popular bar that one of their ghouls run; and so on.<br /> <br /> If the PCs just need a place to hang out, that isn't something the ST actually needs to create. The PCs can create the description, and the ST just needs to approve it (perhaps revising it as needed before approval).<br /> <br /> Things that the ST would need to create are those locations that are part of the greater chronicle setting itself. Examples might be established mortal artistic or cultural institutions that nevertheless host Elysiums. A special nightclub controlled by a vampire that is Masquerade friendly where Hunting rolls are at lower difficulty. A location like the above for PCs' sets, but belonging to an NPC vampire or coterie that is a place the PCs could easily discover to meet an NPC.<br /> <br /> It'll be the ST created locations where the PCs will go out to meet other vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Internetflexing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition#post1563206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Elysium's always in effect as hang out spots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Elysium can be any place or event that the Prince (or perhaps the greater vampire community by consensus that the Prince simply acknowledges) wants to be an Elysium. So a museum might be a permanent Elysium where any time a vampire visits, that vampire knows the Elysium rules are in effect. Or it could be a permanent location, but the Elysium rules only apply on a specific weeknight, holiday, or other regular schedule when events are hosted there (maybe a session of the Prince's court, celebration of an important anniversary to the local Kindred, a regularly scheduled party thrown by the local Toreador salon, etc.) Or they could be special one time events whose location and dates are established in advanced and communicated to the greater Kindred community.<br /> <br /> Some domains might have many Elysiums. Many locations designated as such, and many parties and events. Another domain might not have any Elysiums established although I think most domains will have at least 1-3. It all depends on the culture of the local domain (like which clans are most dominant or powerful) and how much power the Prince and his supporters have to enforce the sanctity of Elysium. A Prince who promotes lots of Elysiums better have the power to protect all of them, or she risks looking weak whenever some jackass flaunts the rules.<br /> <br /> So as the ST, you have a lot of flexibility in terms of how you want to handle this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Internetflexing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition#post1563206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there vampire run clubs or secret places mostly vamps frequent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There are lots of canonical places described in many sourcebooks. These places may or may not be Elysium. However, the most popular places probably either have open or secret protection by one or more of the domain's power brokers, or are at least frequented by Kindred who respect the place enough for it to be safe (most of the time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T07:11:12-07:00","id":1563783,"title":"","content":"As others have said, unless you're forcing the Coterie's hand by having a powerful NPC invite/force them to a particular place, it might be better to let the players decide where they hang out.<br /> <br /> But that's probably less than helpful for a new ST, and it makes it harder (though hardly impossible) to make the &quot;set&quot; memorable.<br /> <br /> One thing to consider is letting the players decide, but giving them parameters in which they need to work. Like &quot;the meeting spot needs to be a spot open to the public at night&quot;, or conversely &quot;it needs to be NOT open to the public at night&quot;. It depends on what purpose you need the location for. Which I think is the ACTUAL question you need to answer: If this is where the Chronicle starts (&quot;you start in a tavern&quot; style), what's leading the Coterie into the initial plot hook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T18:19:48-07:00","id":1563792,"title":"","content":"I've always tried to treat the Coterie (or Pack, Cabal, etc.) as a character in and of itself, one that all of the players help create together. Everyone talks about which parts of the game/setting they are most interested in and want to explore, and try to work out a group concept everyone can agree on. Said concept can be pretty broad, and even multi-focused. Typical focuses include, but aren't limited to:<ul><li>Clan - everyone is the same Clan, obviously. And this clearly doesn't apply here, but various examples are in the backs of the revised Clanbooks</li> <li>Combat - Muscle for hire, body guards, a particular elder (or the Prince/Sheriff)'s hunting dogs, thrill seekers, or some other reason.</li> <li>Scholarly - Noddists, conspiracy theorists, art collectors, research scientists, information brokers, academics, etc.</li> <li>Financial - Making money, be it legally or not, either for its own ends or as a method of accumulating power or living an extravagant un-lifestyle.</li> <li>Politics - Working together to accumulate politics power and influence, both among mortals and the Kindred, as political fixers, Harpies, negotiators, or community organizers.</li> <li>Crime - The group is essentially a budding criminal syndicate looking to expand their turf.</li> <li>Lifestyle - Everyone shares a similar hobby or pursuit, be it underground gladiatorial games, street racing, cutting edge fashion, computer technology, boardgames, shared religious beliefs, common ethnicity/culture, or any of a million other things.</li> </ul><br /> The place they gather will serve as a hangout, headquarters, barracks, safe house, place of business, or whatever else depending on what the Coterie does. It can potentially act as a shared Haven or even as starting Domain they've carved out for themselves (or been granted by a potential patron). Random ideas just off the top of my head:<ul><li>A rundown nightclub that's seen better days but could potentially become the next big thing for the Rack and potentially a future Elysium</li> <li>A private hospital or asylum that offers both a quiet and secluded hideout and a source of food</li> <li>A mostly abandoned train yard full of the rusting hulks of forgotten train cars (railway or subway) that offers privacy and defense</li> <li>One of the city's remaining War on Poverty era public housing projects that has been turned into an urban fortress</li> <li>An abandoned church, that can be kept as is or renovated into something else (night club, museum, etc.)</li> <li>An antique books store that brings in a source of revenue, intellectual contacts, and a certain degree of prestige when other vampires come looking for rare tomes</li> <li>A minor league baseball park that can host night games, making it a potential Rack or Elysium</li> <li>A chop shop that is the center of a city wide car theft ring.</li> <li>One of the city's smaller ethnic enclaves from which all or most of the Coterie are connected to</li> <li>A local radio station, one of the few not owned by a nationwide conglomerate and able to program its own music, which makes it a potential way for the city's Kindred to communicate with each other</li> <li>A lost subway station, one built decades or even a century ago and no longer on any city maps</li> <li>A forgotten Cold War bomb shelter</li> <li>An abandoned Gilded Age mansion, one that is somehow still standing and has a reputation for being haunted</li> <li>An RV that the Coterie uses to roam about the city and squat at different locations during daylight hours</li> </ul><br /> As to the question of &quot;are their vampire run clubs?&quot;, the answer is yes. First edition gave us Chicago's Succubus Club and San Fransisco's Vampire Club (run by a vampire Oscar Wilde of all people), so they've always been a part of the game and setting. See also the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vampires from Anne Rice's<i> Interview with the Vampire</i>. These places tend to serve as part of the Rack, an Elysium, or both. (While perhaps slightly dated at this point, the first Blade movie offers a number of locations that would work really well as potential Kindred hangouts.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-02T19:13:58-07:00","id":1563793,"title":"","content":"Los Angeles also has the Asylum, run by the Voerman Sisters. It's not strictly a space for vampires, but this is actually an example of how varied can be the places where vampires gather, not just on the type of space but also on how much they're expected to adapt to it rather than have it built to cater to them.<br /> <br /> I've noticed, by the way, that even in D&amp;D I have never used the &quot;you meet at a tavern&quot; starting scene. I usually start with the scattered group being brought together one by one according to the plot.<br /> <br /> My last D&amp;D game started with everyone being part of a detective agency specialized in lost person and divorce related cases. The plot is apocalyptic, but the phenomena started being confused with running children.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking about starting a game where the group will be in a tavern, but as employees.<br /> <br /> VtM isn't much different, and my next game will start with the group being linked by mortal blood, they're all members of the game family Embraced around the same time, but not by the same clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 09-03-2026, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T15:00:13-07:00","id":1563810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1563206-first-time-st-best-starting-hangouts-for-my-coterie-first-second-edition?p=1563793#post1563793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Los Angeles also has the Asylum, run by the Voerman Sisters. It's not strictly a space for vampires, but this is actually an example of how varied can be the places where vampires gather, not just on the type of space but also on how much they're expected to adapt to it rather than have it built to cater to them.<br /> <br /> I've noticed, by the way, that even in D&amp;D I have never used the &quot;you meet at a tavern&quot; starting scene. I usually start with the scattered group being brought together one by one according to the plot.<br /> <br /> My last D&amp;D game started with everyone being part of a detective agency specialized in lost person and divorce related cases. The plot is apocalyptic, but the phenomena started being confused with running children.<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking about starting a game where the group will be in a tavern, but as employees.<br /> <br /> VtM isn't much different, and my next game will start with the group being linked by mortal blood, they're all members of the game family Embraced around the same time, but not by the same clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd forgotten about the Asylum. I don't have any of my books handy, but I seem to recall that several of the 2nd ed City by Night books had at least one vampire-owned social gathering place. I think Requiem's Damnation City sourcebook talked about the topic at some point as well. (Honestly, given Justin Achilli's love of night clubs and bars, I was always surprised the revised edition didn't have an entire book devoted to what vampires do every night just to hang out, socialize, and network.)<br /> <br /> And PC detective agency is such a perfect starting point for a lot of games. I really lament that there was never a World of Darkness: Private Eyes book back in the day, as it works so well for all the game lines and as a Hunters Hunted expansion. <br /> <br /> Another suggestion I remember from one of the early Vampire books is having the PCs all having been presented to Kindred society at the same time, and have sort of become a Coterie by default. I suspect that this may have been adapted from what was considered the default Werewolf set up of having the PCs all undergo their Rite of Passages together and then get stuck together as a Pack. <br /> <br /> (I've noticed that almost every D&amp;D/MMO influenced fantasy anime defaults to the Adventurers' Guild trope. I'd kind of like to see at least one go totally old school where the main character is forced to hang out in and eventually work at a tavern in the hopes of finding profitable quests to go on.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-03T20:13:49-07:00","id":1563817,"title":"","content":"Yes Vampire The Requiem Damnation City would be a valuable asset for coming up for world building your city and what areas the sects and clans have their holdings and VTM has a more recent source book that I think is called Live from the Succubus Club and and it could be used for ideas for where your coterie can hang out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-04T11:35:42-07:00","id":1563833,"title":"","content":"I should add that Tattered Facades could give you ideas for hangouts for your cotorie and the possible supporting cast suggestions to flesh out your setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}